    "title": "Crimson Tide to take on struggling Rebels in Oxford - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By AJ Holliday ,\n1 days ago\nOXFORD, Miss. ( WIAT ) — Alabama basketball is on the road again Wednesday as it prepares for a showdown against Ole Miss.\nThe Crimson Tide will now be without Charles Bediako, whose request for a preliminary injunction was denied Monday . In the Crimson Tide’s last game, it was an impressive 96-92 win against rival Auburn in the Iron Bowl of Basketball.\nLabaron Philon led the team with 25 points, and freshman Amari Allen contributed 17 points. Bama improved to 16-7 overall and 6-4 in conference play.\nCollege basketball career of Charles Bediako ends as Alabama judge denies injunction request It’s been a long season for the Rebels, who come into the game with an 11-12 record and 3-7 mark in SEC play. Ole Miss has lost five straight games, and its most recent contest was a double-digit loss to Texas. AJ Storr leads the team in scoring, averaging 13.7 points a game.\nTipoff is scheduled for 6 p.m. Wednesday on SEC Network.\nCopyright 2026 Nexstar Media, Inc. All rights reserved. This material may not be published, broadcast, rewritten, or redistributed. For the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to CBS 42.",
